(version 1)

# Custom DRC rules for the DIGITAL artwork of the CNC-milled vinyl ADC.
#
# Copper is isolation-milled with an 0.8 mm flat end mill, so 0.8 mm is the hard
# floor on any copper-to-copper gap: the tool cannot enter anything narrower, and
# a gap it cannot enter stays shorted. The Default netclass asks for 0.85 mm --
# the `cnc` fabrication profile's number, which KiCad-Autoplace also stamps into
# the .kicad_pro -- leaving every routed track ~0.025 mm of copper either side of
# the cut as margin for runout and registration.
#
# Every footprint here was audited against that floor. Only the 2.54 mm headers
# sit between the tool diameter and the netclass clearance:
#
#   J1   PinHeader_1x03_P2.54mm_Vertical  -> 0.84 mm pad-to-pad  (4 pairs)
#   J2   PinHeader_1x08_P2.54mm_Vertical  -> 0.84 mm pad-to-pad  (14 pairs)
#   J4   PinHeader_2x08_P2.54mm_Vertical  -> 0.84 mm pad-to-pad  (30 pairs)
#
# That gap is set by each header's own 2.54 mm pin pitch, not by anything we cut,
# and it still clears the tool in a single pass. The rules below relax the
# clearance ONLY between two items that both belong to one of those footprints.
# The full 0.85 mm stays in force between different components and for every
# track.
#
# Needing no exception: the DIP-8/14/16 LongPads sockets at 0.94 mm, and the
# five 100n discs at 3.4 mm.

(rule "J1_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('J1') && B.memberOfFootprint('J1')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))

(rule "J2_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('J2') && B.memberOfFootprint('J2')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))

(rule "J4_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('J4') && B.memberOfFootprint('J4')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))
